.begin choose bold
	Guden received a new toy for Christmas.   He was very big
and had eight legs.  He was very young and had brown-black hair covering his body. 
The toy was very complicated and came with a thick instruction booklet.
It was a new model and had a 
viewing screen, a power unit, a computing circuit and a
complex control board.  
He knew he would
like his new toy even though it was "educational".
	He chose a disk from a box and inserted
it in a slot on the side of his new toy.  He hooked up the power unit
then turned it on.
.skip 2
.choose normal
	Jorden was an Earthling.  If you call someone born
in the 95th century who has never seen Earth or Sol an
Earthling.  Jorden was a human being.  If you call someone
who is only a brain that sits inside a concrete-like box with
wires running in and out of it a human being.  Jorden 
wasn't very upset about just being a brain for he had a
choice of many bodies.  In addition, he was safe and immortal.
	It had taken him a couple of thousand years of occupying the bodies of
men, women, dogs, fish, Venusian cloud creatures, jet subs,
space ships, computers, and a few imaginary computer-simulated
bodies to get bored.  Not many imaginary bodies though,
for he was old-fashioned and preferred the real thing.
He received the input to the body (or bodies) by radio
waves which were converted to electrical nerve impulses
and sent to the appropriate sections of the brain.  In a similar manner, he could
send signals to control whatever body he was occupying.
Two thousands years of it and he was bored. He wanted to
do something no one else had.  But anything within light
years someone had been or done.
	He decided to go to the edge of the universe.  No one
had ever gone that far before.  To go would take billions of
Earth years Milky Way time and all he had known would be
gone if he chose to come back.  Besides all that, it would be 
dangerous----he would have to take his brain along or else
it would take billions of years.  But were he to travel
with an acceleration of 3 or 4 times Earth's gravity, then within two weeks he would
be approaching the speed of light and time would slow down
(relative to Milky Way time).  And were he to continue accelerating
for a couple of years, then a second to him would equal thousands
of years to those on Earth.
	He set off.
.skip 2
.choose bold
	Guden flicked on the viewer switch and the screen lit
up with a white dot in the middle.  He fiddled with the
viewing controls and zoomed up on the dot.  The dot was a
sun and other dots were lighting up forming a growing sphere
of stars.  He set the viewer for random close-up periphery
search and sat back on his hind four legs and watched.  The
screen went blank for a second and then a solar system appeared.
The screen went white as it zoomed in on the sun.  Then it
focused on the first planet.  A yellow white sphere kept
growing and then a small lake appeared and it grew.  Soon
green water filled the screen.  A fish-like creature swam by
and the screen focused on the creature's head.
Its eye grew and filled the
screen.  The screen became greenish purple with two
red-orange dots near the center.  As the dots grew one attacked
and ate the other.  The bloated red-orange organism filled
the screen.  A black oval within it grew and filled the screen.
A vibrating molecule appeared and filled the screen.  Next appeared
an atom with jumping electrons, then its nucleus filled
the screen.  Then the screen displayed a proton and then just vibrating, spinning
shapes and colors.  Then it went blank, and after a pause a white dot appeared and the
sequence repeated----though always providing a different show.
.skip 2
.choose normal
	Jorden was in his third year of his voyage.  His time
flow was almost zero.  His relativistic mass was approaching
that of a galaxy. If a Milky Way observer could see him
his length would be measured in microns.  But to Jorden
all was fine but for the colors of stars and planets his
scope picked up.  He figured he should be getting near the
edge of the universe soon, about seventeen billion light
years from Earth.  
	The scope showed an Earth-type planet orbiting a
chartreuse sun.  As it zoomed in on the planet's surface
he saw a highly technological society.  He zeroed in on
an urban area at the tip of a lake.  He experienced a feeling of [fi]deja
vu[fn] as the scope showed the residential section with
balloon-like residences.  Then it came to him----he had
seen a very similar scene only a few days ago.  His scope
lost its fix as the distance increased.
.skip 2
.choose bold
	Guden got bored of his new toy.  He left it on and
went looking for other Christmas toys.  The viewer kept
zooming in on differing periphery systems.  Some worlds
were baren, some were highly technological.  A
rhythmic sound started and a repeating pattern arose on the
viewer.  Every sequence was identical to one 327
sequences prior.
.skip
.choose normal
	Jorden worked his scope feverishly.  He felt that he was going
around in circles.  He saw a planet and two and
a half days later he saw the same planet.  He was 
perplexed----how could he be going around in circles?
Was space warped? Could he ever reach the edge?
Would he ever break the loop?
.skip 2
.choose bold
	Guden found no good new toys.  He went back to his
toy.  He heard the thumping and saw that the disk was 
defective and was repeating.  He gave it a tap and then
decided to use a different disk.  He pulled out the old
one.
.skip 2
.choose normal
	Jorden finally stopped seeing the same planets 
repeating.  Jorden stopped seeing anything at all.
Jorden and his universe no longer existed.
.skip 2
.choose bold
	Guden put in another disk. It wasn't a bad present
he thought.
